          "Synchronously acquire PH and VIN at the IC pads relative to pin 6, with local high-impedance active differential probes and no long ground clip. Establish the full D103 input, thermal and current conditions independently.",
          "Set logic load to 145-150 mA and verify peak inductor current at most 0.81 A. Settle for at least 50 ms and verify output stability before acquiring at least 1 ms continuously.",
          "Evaluate high level relative to synchronous VIN and low level relative to GND. Plateau statistics exclude 50 ns around edges; all raw samples remain included in peak and excursion checks. Require measurable high and low plateaus.",
          "Rise/fall times use 10-90 percent of measured plateau levels. Positive excursion threshold is relative to VIN; negative threshold is relative to GND. Merge excursions separated by at most 2 ns before duration evaluation.",
          "Record instrument calibration, gain, offset, probe loading and actual voltage/time uncertainty. Entire uncertainty intervals must lie within acceptance limits; boundary overlap is inconclusive and requires retest. Negative excursions including timing uncertainty must remain strictly shorter than 10 ns.",
